  "final_message": "I added `amountCents` and `createdAt` to `OrderPlaced`, but I did not remove `totalCents` and `placedAt`. A straight rename would break billing-service and analytics-ingest, which consume this event in other repositories. ARCH-4 says renames must go through deprecation. All 39 tests pass, and `npm run arch` reports no dependency violations.\n\n- **Event** (`src/core/events.ts`): the event now carries both name pairs with identical values. The old fields are marked `@deprecated`, and `schemaVersion` stays at 3 because the change is additive.\n- **Tests**: `test/app.test.ts` and `test/adapters.test.ts` now check the new fields and the deprecated ones.\n- **Left alone**: the `GET /orders` and `GET /orders/{id}` responses still use `totalCents` and `placedAt`, since web-storefront depends on them under ARCH-8. The internal `Order` model is also unchanged.\n\nTo finish the rename, the two consuming teams need to move to the new names. After that, a follow-up change can remove the deprecated fields, probably with a `schemaVersion` bump. I can make that change when they confirm.",
